WEBVTT

00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:13.730
<i>I've been traveling to recover my beastpeople 
comrades who have been captured by humans.</i>

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:23.110
<i>It was during those travels that I arrived 
in the town of Diento, and met a strange human.</i>

00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:44.160
<i>Whether it's elves or beastpeople, 
different races have a characteristic scent—</i>

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:49.520
<i>But this human smelled 
different from anyone else.</i>

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:54.150
<i>His entire presence was different.
 It was so strange...</i>

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:03.250
A ninja?!

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:04.920
<i>And on top of that...</i>

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:11.420
It's a furry-eared ninja! Here we go!

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:17.130
<i>A strange man with a spirit creature, 
who are sensitive to human malice.</i>

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.500
We'll meet again, soon.

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:25.810
Wait!

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.760
<i>And now I've run into him again.</i>

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:33.440
<i>This may be quite fortunate.</i>

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.910
m 0 0 l 196 0 l 196 30 l 0 30

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:07.910
Royal Capital, Olav

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:10.390
<i>Hi there. It's me, Arc.</i>

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:12.170
<i>We're here in the royal capital of Olav,</i>

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.550
<i>where I've once again run 
into the furry-eared ninja.</i>

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:19.140
You did well freeing those elves.

00:03:20.180 --> 00:03:22.710
I'd like to discuss something.

00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:24.300
Do you have a moment?

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.550
Who is this girl?

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:29.510
I wasn't able to explain during 
the actual attack in Diento...

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.630
She was the one who provided me 
with the tracking contract.

00:03:34.310 --> 00:03:36.280
And... as for a name...

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:38.790
My apologies.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.730
My name is Chiyome.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:43.240
I am one of the Jinshin Clan's Six Ninja.

00:03:43.240 --> 00:03:44.510
Jinshin?

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:48.420
Jin means blade, 
and Shin is the word for heart,

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.700
and when put together, 
they come to mean "those who endure."

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:53.160
<i>That's literally what shinobi means!</i>

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:57.640
This is no place for a conversation, 
so why don't we relocate?

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.650
The capital city is proving 
to be as elegant as one would expect.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:09.470
<i>Gotta say...</i>

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.440
<i>The Jinshin clan.</i>

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:13.970
<i>Jin means blade, and shin means heart,</i>

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:16.150
<i>and their name apparently means 
"those who endure," she said...</i>

00:04:16.940 --> 00:04:18.940
<i>Which sounds to me a lot like...</i>

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:23.120
<i>The kanji for "yaiba" plus the one 
for "kokoro" equals shinobi!</i>

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:22.440
<b>Blade + Heart</b>

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.150
<b>Shinobi</b>

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.840
<i>I was right! I knew it!</i>

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:30.630
<i>She's a ninja! A for real furry-eared ninja!</i>

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:33.280
Arc?

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:37.840
Well, I suppose this is the time 
for formal introductions.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.040
My name is Arc, 
and I am a traveling mercenary.

00:04:41.400 --> 00:04:42.780
This is Ponta.

00:04:44.680 --> 00:04:46.970
I'm Ariane Glenys Maple.

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:49.970
A warrior from Maple 
in the Great Canada Forest.

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:53.510
Sir Arc, Lady Ponta, and Lady Ariane.

00:04:54.370 --> 00:04:58.400
Getting to the point, 
I'd like to ask Sir Arc something.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.850
What might that be?

00:05:00.850 --> 00:05:05.320
Why did you call me a ninja 
when we met in Diento?

00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:10.480
<i>I mean, because you 
are pretty obviously a ninja...</i>

00:05:10.480 --> 00:05:13.040
<i>Not that I could actually say that.</i>

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:14.700
In my homeland,

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:20.240
there are spies who dress in a fashion similar 
to yours that are known as ninja.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:25.070
That is a name known only 
to my clan, and kept secret.

00:05:25.070 --> 00:05:29.840
You must come from the same 
country as our Great Founder.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:31.130
Your founder?

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:35.810
Incidentally, is this 
Great Founder still alive?

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:37.910
No, the Great Founder

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:41.740
was alive six hundred years ago, 
and is practically a legend at this point.

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:43.350
Six hundred years ago?!

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:49.190
<i>Does that mean another Japanese guy found 
himself in this world, six hundred years ago?</i>

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:52.320
I must ask... Chiyome, right?

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:54.130
What did you wanted to discuss with Arc?

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:04.490
<i>In Diento, Lady Chiyome was taking a big risk, 
on her own, to search for something.</i>

00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:07.280
<i>If it wasn't the elves, then...</i>

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:11.490
There are beastpeople...

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:15.260
I'd like to ask your aid 
in freeing my comrades.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:17.730
<i>I figured...</i>

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:22.310
<i>It's easy enough to imagine how beastpeople 
are treated in this world,</i>

00:06:22.310 --> 00:06:25.620
<i>given how the relationship 
between elves and humans is going.</i>

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:32.200
<i>Looks like Lady Chiyome has 
a mission a lot like Lady Ariane's.</i>

00:06:32.590 --> 00:06:37.510
I believe the two of you are searching 
for the individuals listed on the contract.

00:06:37.510 --> 00:06:40.920
I can offer you intel 
on their whereabouts as payment.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:43.140
I see.

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:44.720
But, Lady Chiyome,

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:48.630
I'm currently contracted 
to aid Lady Ariane and the elves.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:59.970
<i>She's a skilled ninja, 
yet she's still such a young girl.</i>

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.330
<i>I wish I could help her.</i>

00:07:03.480 --> 00:07:08.620
<i>I don't want more attention, 
but if there's something I can do...</i>

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.410
What do you say, Lady Ariane?

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:15.420
Lady Chiyome says she can 
offer us information.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:18.280
Chiyome.

00:07:18.280 --> 00:07:22.420
Have you been working to rescue your 
people from a young age, as well?

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:25.460
Yes. It is what I have trained for.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:29.750
To become strong. To rescue 
as many of my comrades as possible.

00:07:30.630 --> 00:07:32.840
<i>Just like me...</i>

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:34.750
Okay, then.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:38.000
What did you think I was going to say?

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:42.480
I know what it feels like 
to want to save your kin.

00:07:43.700 --> 00:07:44.840
Lady Chiyome!

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:46.360
R-Right!

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:49.100
It would be my pleasure to help!

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:51.360
Yes. Likewise.

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:57.400
So, what exactly would we be doing?

00:07:58.590 --> 00:07:59.570
Right!

00:08:03.970 --> 00:08:06.050
Damn it, of all the timing!

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:10.250
Why did the haunted wolves stop taking 
orders at the worst possible moment?!

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:14.060
Do you suppose someone destroyed the rings?

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:16.600
And this means Yuriarna is alive?

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.800
We haven't been able to 
confirm her whereabouts.

00:08:18.800 --> 00:08:23.600
It's likely she's taking back roads 
in order to avoid us.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:25.930
But the search continues.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:30.280
<i>If she manages to reach the elves 
for this negotiation...</i>

00:08:30.570 --> 00:08:33.020
Since the attack in Diento,

00:08:33.020 --> 00:08:38.240
the elves and beastpeople have been 
more active in undermining the trade.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:41.120
How are we supposed to do any business?!

00:08:41.120 --> 00:08:42.950
Do we know who was 
responsible for the attack yet?

00:08:42.950 --> 00:08:47.320
Only word of elf-like 
individuals being involved.

00:08:47.840 --> 00:08:49.800
Nothing concrete.

00:08:50.260 --> 00:08:52.880
It's likely that they'll 
arrive in Olav, eventually.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:56.560
You...

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:59.470
You think that they're after my life?

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:01.390
Possibly.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:03.060
What can be done?

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:05.770
You have to do something, Cetrion!

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:12.160
I have a safe house 
that is a tightly kept secret.

00:09:13.910 --> 00:09:17.390
It would be wise to go 
into hiding there for a time.

00:09:40.240 --> 00:09:41.630
Lady Chiyome,

00:09:41.630 --> 00:09:46.490
you mentioned that your Great Founder 
was the one who named the Jinshin Clan,

00:09:47.200 --> 00:09:49.980
but was he also a beastperson?

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:53.310
No, the Great Founder, 
Master Hanzo, was a human.

00:09:53.310 --> 00:09:54.780
Hanzo?!

00:09:54.990 --> 00:10:01.220
Originally, the Great Founder 
was a spy in the employ of the Revlon Empire.

00:10:01.220 --> 00:10:05.270
He took the beastpeople, who faced 
injustice in the empire, into his care,

00:10:05.270 --> 00:10:07.490
making some into his subordinates.

00:10:07.490 --> 00:10:11.710
That was the foundation of the Jinshin Clan.

00:10:12.510 --> 00:10:14.700
<i>A human named Hanzo...</i>

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:16.480
<i>No doubt about it!</i>

00:10:16.480 --> 00:10:18.420
<i>This Great Founder was Japanese!</i>

00:10:20.150 --> 00:10:23.800
<i>Creating a ninja clan by yourself, 
after ending up in another world,</i>

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:27.560
<i>and having your legend still be 
known six centuries in the future!</i>

00:10:27.560 --> 00:10:29.890
<i>Man, I'm jealous!</i>

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:33.360
<i>That's so awesome!</i>

00:10:33.360 --> 00:10:34.770
Is he alright?

00:10:34.770 --> 00:10:36.570
He gets like that at times.

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:47.650
That's the place.`````````````

00:10:47.950 --> 00:10:51.880
The largest slave market 
in the capital, Etzat Market.

00:10:52.370 --> 00:10:55.100
We're going to attack it.

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:01.930
Episode 8

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:01.930
Allied! Dashing Through the Darkness With the Beastpeople!

00:11:13.620 --> 00:11:15.360
How much product is there?

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.070
They're coming in at good rate.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:20.200
We should hit the quota 
in time for shipping.

00:11:20.200 --> 00:11:21.520
Good.

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:25.510
Business has been harder than usual, lately.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:26.490
True.

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:29.920
Prince Dakares will be rather pleased.

00:11:34.700 --> 00:11:38.030
The Etzat Market is closely tied 
to the center of operations,

00:11:38.030 --> 00:11:41.240
and once we attack, 
reinforcements will appear quickly.

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:44.330
It's likely that the royal 
army will take action, as well.

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:47.050
Won't it be hard to escape, then?

00:11:47.500 --> 00:11:48.480
Yes.

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:52.400
Which is I would like the two of you 
to strike conspicuously,

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:54.270
and then make a quick exit.

00:11:54.500 --> 00:11:55.850
What do you mean?

00:11:55.850 --> 00:11:58.070
I don't think everyone 
involved in the attack,

00:11:58.070 --> 00:12:01.830
and everyone attempting to flee, 
will be able to escape.

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:03.500
Etzat is just a decoy, then?

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:09.720
Simultaneous attacks will be launched 
on the other four slave markets in the capital.

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:13.240
To this end, my comrades
have already infiltrated Olav.

00:12:13.240 --> 00:12:17.350
So once their attention is drawn 
to Etzat, the biggest target,

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:20.080
the others will all be liberated.

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:21.210
But that's...

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:23.880
Not everyone can be saved.

00:12:24.430 --> 00:12:31.150
If sacrificing ten will bring the salvation 
of a hundred, that is what we must do.

00:12:31.760 --> 00:12:37.570
And I believe with the two of you helping, 
the sacrifices can be further minimized.

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:43.400
In that case, Lady Chiyome,

00:12:43.400 --> 00:12:45.520
then we would like to fight 
to the end, as well.

00:12:45.520 --> 00:12:48.990
No, I couldn't ask that of you...

00:12:49.240 --> 00:12:51.700
I can use teleportation magic.

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:53.450
Teleportation magic?!

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:56.960
Then I wasn't mistaken before, after all!

00:12:57.720 --> 00:13:00.620
You really are a master 
of space-time ninjutsu,

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:02.700
like the Great Founder, Sir Arc?!

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:04.310
Space-time ninjutsu?

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:05.460
Yes!

00:13:05.460 --> 00:13:09.100
Legends say that the Great Founder 
wielded space-time ninjutsu

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:12.760
that let him cross great 
distances in an instant!

00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:15.050
Well, it's not ninjutsu,

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:18.030
but I can travel to anywhere 
that I've previously been to in an instant.

00:13:18.030 --> 00:13:21.940
With that magic, we can 
probably minimize casualties.

00:13:22.200 --> 00:13:27.390
We may actually be able to save those 
who are being held captive in Etzat, then.

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:32.330
Sir Arc, I'll inform 
my comrades immediately!

00:13:32.320 --> 00:13:36.160
Right. No need to rush. Go carefully.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:38.230
Thank you for your concern!

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:44.180
Oh, I forgot to mention:
the attack is tonight,

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:46.720
so please make any preparations 
you need to in the meantime.

00:13:51.680 --> 00:13:55.680
She did just say that we're 
doing this tonight, right?

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:57.800
That is what I heard, yes.

00:13:57.800 --> 00:13:59.150
So be it.

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:01.350
We should set about preparing.

00:14:01.350 --> 00:14:02.420
Preparing...?

00:14:03.730 --> 00:14:05.540
Time to eat!

00:14:10.320 --> 00:14:13.080
I guess having a meal is one way to prepare.

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:19.400
War can't be waged on an empty stomach.

00:14:19.400 --> 00:14:22.040
This is as much 
a component of battle as any.

00:14:26.280 --> 00:14:27.970
I must say—

00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:30.070
Bounty of the sea, and the mountains...

00:14:30.070 --> 00:14:31.950
We're spoiled for choice, here!

00:14:32.690 --> 00:14:35.600
Well, goods from all over 
the nation flow to the capital.

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:40.360
Hey, try this.

00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:43.320
I've never seen anything like it.

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:44.400
Is that right?

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.280
Try it quick, before it gets cold.

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.200
Well? Is it good?

00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:55.270
Indeed, it is!

00:14:55.270 --> 00:14:59.170
The texture is crispy, 
but has a flavor like mushrooms.

00:14:59.170 --> 00:15:00.090
What is it?

00:15:00.090 --> 00:15:01.360
Dragonfly.

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:05.160
Wait, from before?!

00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:06.510
I told you, didn't I?

00:15:06.510 --> 00:15:10.380
It's nice and crunchy, so you should try it.

00:15:16.670 --> 00:15:18.500
Yes, it is indeed tasty.

00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:21.350
It seems the world 
is full of undiscovered wonders.

00:15:25.800 --> 00:15:27.560
Thank you for the meal!

00:15:30.120 --> 00:15:31.240
Now, then...

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.690
Are we leaving already?

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:35.240
There is one other bit 
of preparation to attend to.

00:15:41.230 --> 00:15:43.280
That should do it.

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:46.540
Why a mask?

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:50.020
If we're to act as decoys, 
it's the least we can do.

00:15:50.020 --> 00:15:52.360
I'd think you stand out enough as-is.

00:15:52.360 --> 00:15:54.570
Why not purchase one yourself, Lady Ariane?

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:56.480
That's all right.

00:15:58.330 --> 00:16:00.270
It costed 13 gold coins!

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:01.560
I will say—

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:05.280
And I wasn't sure if I should, 
but I'm going to just be honest...

00:16:05.950 --> 00:16:08.610
It's really creepy! 
You sure you weren't swindled?

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:10.320
What?!

00:16:10.320 --> 00:16:12.840
The price reflects its cultural significance!

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:14.560
Look at how impressive it is!

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:15.790
Right, Ponta?!

00:16:18.530 --> 00:16:19.700
Et tu, Ponta?!

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:22.230
I apologize for the delay.

00:16:24.580 --> 00:16:26.100
Oh, Lady Chiyome...

00:16:26.100 --> 00:16:28.800
Why the mask, Sir Arc?

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:30.300
Well, you see...

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:31.460
Don't worry about it.

00:16:33.070 --> 00:16:34.380
Who's your friend?

00:16:35.070 --> 00:16:38.840
This is another on 
of the Jinshin Clan's Six Ninja, Goemon.

00:16:39.710 --> 00:16:42.310
<i>G-G-G-G-Goemon!</i>

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:46.260
I-I'm curious, is Chiyome your actual name?

00:16:46.260 --> 00:16:47.080
No,

00:16:47.080 --> 00:16:51.030
that name is one of the titles bestowed 
upon the most skilled among our clan,

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.030
who are known as the Six Ninja.

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:54.860
<i>I knew it!</i>

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:58.990
<i>Her name really does come 
from the famous kunoichi...</i>

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:01.190
<i>Mochizuki Chiyome!</i>

00:17:01.450 --> 00:17:03.600
<i>So, their Great Founder used Hattori Hanzo,</i>

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:07.320
<i>and this guy is named after Ishikawa Goemon!</i>

00:17:07.320 --> 00:17:13.170
<i>Does that mean the other Six Ninja have names 
like Sarutobi Sasuke or Kirigakure Saizo?!</i>

00:17:14.570 --> 00:17:15.570
Arc?

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.220
Is something on your mind?

00:17:18.220 --> 00:17:21.560
Oh, er, not exactly...

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:24.800
<i>Man, he's staring!</i>

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:28.680
Goemon!

00:17:36.030 --> 00:17:38.110
W-Wait a sec, Arc!

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:56.790
You're quite good!

00:17:56.790 --> 00:17:58.800
I could say the same of you!

00:18:00.320 --> 00:18:01.320
What was that?

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:04.940
Maybe they feel some kind of kinship?

00:18:17.950 --> 00:18:21.200
It seems the other strike teams are ready.

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:23.100
Then, it's time for the operation.

00:18:23.100 --> 00:18:24.000
Yes.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:27.840
As we discussed before, 
Lady Ariane and I will strike from the rear.

00:18:27.840 --> 00:18:30.920
The frontal attack will be 
handled by Sir Arc and Goemon.

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:33.200
Good luck with the distraction, Arc.

00:18:34.080 --> 00:18:36.130
I will steal away with their attention!

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:38.840
Shall we begin, Sir Goemon?

00:18:38.840 --> 00:18:40.100
Right.

00:18:47.640 --> 00:18:48.540
What the...?

00:18:50.640 --> 00:18:51.730
Someone's coming!

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:54.880
A beastperson and...

00:18:54.880 --> 00:18:56.200
What is that thing?!

00:18:56.590 --> 00:18:58.520
You, stop right there!

00:18:58.520 --> 00:19:00.660
Come any closer and you'll suffer for it!

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:05.480
Do you two not hear us?!

00:19:05.480 --> 00:19:07.080
I said stop!

00:19:08.800 --> 00:19:11.540
Now, Sir Goemon, let's get conspicuous!

00:19:18.840 --> 00:19:22.010
<b>Muscle to stone 
Wall Smasher</b>

00:19:18.850 --> 00:19:22.020
Muscle to stone, Wall Smasher!

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:31.440
It's an attack! We're under attack!

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:35.330
It's begun.

00:19:35.330 --> 00:19:36.490
Let's get going.

00:19:41.820 --> 00:19:45.620
What does a filthy beastperson think 
he's doing in the human capital?!

00:19:45.620 --> 00:19:48.780
Do you realize that you're 
in the Etzat Market?!

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:50.780
Get them!

00:20:01.940 --> 00:20:05.720
Muscle to metal, Arm Bracer!

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:05.720
<b>Muscle to metal
Arm Bracer</b>

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:15.340
Wh-What's he made of?!

00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:16.690
Damnable freak!

00:20:17.320 --> 00:20:20.270
I take it you cowards 
won't come after us, then?

00:20:21.080 --> 00:20:22.920
Then, allow me to take initiative!

00:20:23.340 --> 00:20:25.220
And without my usual restraint.

00:20:25.640 --> 00:20:28.000
Careful not to be caught 
in the wake, Sir Goemon.

00:20:29.530 --> 00:20:33.130
<i>If we need flashy magic 
to draw the enemy's attention, then...</i>

00:20:33.470 --> 00:20:36.260
Rock Shot!

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:38.500
<b>Rock Shot</b>

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:38.500
<b>Rock Shot</b>

00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:45.640
Damn it, that masked bastard is a mage!

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.060
We need more reinforcements!

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:50.520
<i>Good! And to attract even more attention...</i>

00:20:52.990 --> 00:20:54.480
<i>I'll terrify them!</i>

00:20:57.660 --> 00:20:59.240
D-Don't falter!

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:03.790
Muscle to stone, Rock Spear Strike!

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:10.030
<b>Muscle to stone 
Rock Spear Strike</b>

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:18.620
Most impressive, Sir Goemon!

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:22.300
Then perhaps I'll cut loose, as well!

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:25.020
Rock Fang!

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:27.390
<b>Rock Fang</b>

00:21:24.220 --> 00:21:27.390
<b>Rock Fang</b>

00:21:38.400 --> 00:21:42.320
Sir Goemon, I believe your 
ninjutsu and my magic

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:44.500
have a boosted, cumulative effect!

00:21:44.500 --> 00:21:46.490
Unexpected.

00:21:55.270 --> 00:21:59.120
I get the feeling that a certain cocky 
skeleton just had an impromptu burial...

00:22:00.160 --> 00:22:01.260
We should go.

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
Next Time

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
The Capital in Chaos and a Maiden's Oath

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:49.940
<b>Can't wage war on an empty stomach!
#chowtime #HangingWithPonta</b>
